## Bug

`ggml_backend_openvino_buffer_init_tensor()` in `ggml/src/ggml-openvino/ggml-openvino.cpp` shares `view_src->extra` (the cached OV tensor) with any VIEW tensor, regardless of whether the VIEW has the same shape and data pointer as its source. RESHAPE and offset VIEWs that change `ne` or `data` inherit the wrong OV tensor, causing shape mismatches at inference time.

## Root cause

The current code:

```cpp
if (tensor->view_src != nullptr) {
    if (tensor->view_src->extra != nullptr) {
        tensor->extra = tensor->view_src->extra;
    }
    return GGML_STATUS_SUCCESS;
}
```

This returns early for **all** VIEW tensors, unconditionally sharing the parent's OV tensor. For a RESHAPE (which changes `ne`) or an offset VIEW (which changes `data`), the shared extra has the wrong shape or points to the wrong memory. When OV later uses this extra as an input tensor it sees stale shape metadata and either produces wrong results or aborts.

## Fix

Only share `view_src->extra` when the VIEW is a pure alias — same shape **and** same data pointer:

```cpp
if (tensor->view_src != nullptr) {
    bool can_share = (tensor->data == tensor->view_src->data);
    for (int i = 0; i < GGML_MAX_DIMS && can_share; i++) {
        if (tensor->ne[i] != tensor->view_src->ne[i]) can_share = false;
    }
    if (can_share && tensor->view_src->extra != nullptr) {
        tensor->extra = tensor->view_src->extra;
        return GGML_STATUS_SUCCESS;
    }
    // Fall through to allocate a fresh extra with this tensor's own shape/data.
}
```

## Impact

Affects MoE models (gpt-oss / context-1) where per-expert output tensors are offset VIEWs into a shared MoE output buffer. Each VIEW selects a different expert's slice — different `data` pointer and potentially different `ne` — but all were inheriting the first expert's OV tensor shape. This produced silent wrong values or crashes in the MoE output aggregation.

## Reproduction

Run gpt-oss / context-1-IQ4_NL.gguf with `GGML_OPENVINO_DEVICE=GPU` or `CPU`. MoE output is wrong or the process aborts with a shape mismatch.

