### Summary

When a single token names the same expert in more than one of its `ids` slots,
the CUDA backend disagrees with the CPU reference, and in some shapes dies
with an illegal memory access. `ggml.h` documents no uniqueness requirement on
`ids`, and the CPU backend handles repeats fine, so the two backends currently
implement different semantics.

`tests/test-backend-ops.cpp` never exercises this: `init_mul_mat_id_tensors`
fills each ids row with `i % n_mats` and shuffles it, so within a row the ids
are distinct by construction.

### Reproducer

The patch below adds a `repeat_ids` mode to `test_mul_mat_id` and registers
cases across f16/q8_0/q4_0, batch 1/16/256, broadcast and non-broadcast `b`.
Mode 1 repeats every pair (`data[i] = (i/2) % n_mats`); mode 2 repeats exactly
one pair per row, so that the size of the error shows how much of the output
is affected.

```sh
git apply repeated-ids-repro.patch
cmake --build build --target test-backend-ops -j
./build/bin/test-backend-ops -o MUL_MAT_ID
```

