### Problem description & steps to reproduce

### Problem description

When a draft model is loaded *after* a target model that has consumed
essentially all VRAM, `llama_model::load_tensors` for the draft aborts with:

```
error loading model: invalid vector subscript
```

(`invalid vector subscript` is the MSVC message for `std::vector::at()` out of
range; other STLs would throw `std::out_of_range` or UB.)

The failure depends only on how much VRAM is free when the *draft* starts
loading. On this machine, with the same target and draft:

| `--n-gpu-layers` (target) | result |
|---|---|
| 52 | loads fine |
| 56 | crash |
| 99 | crash |

### Root cause

`src/llama-model.cpp`, in `llama_model::load_tensors`:

```cpp
